.TH VIRTICLE 1 "" "virticle" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
virticle \- web controller for KVM/libvirt hosts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B virticle
[\fIflags\fR]
.br
.B virticle version
.br
.B virticle setup
[\fB\-\-check\fR] [\fB\-\-undo\fR] [\fB\-data\fR \fIdir\fR]
.br
.B virticle node prepare
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIuser\fR@]\fIhost\fR[:\fIport\fR]
.br
.B virticle node unprepare
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIuser\fR@]\fIhost\fR[:\fIport\fR]
.br
.B virticle backup
[\fB\-o\fR \fIfile|dir\fR] [\fB\-\-encrypt\fR] [\fB\-\-passphrase\-file\fR \fIfile\fR]
.br
.B virticle restore
[\fB\-\-passphrase\-file\fR \fIfile\fR] \fIfile\fR
.br
.B virticle web
.BR show | set | reset
[\fB\-data\fR \fIdir\fR] [\fIoptions\fR]
.br
.B virticle user
.BR reset\-2fa | reset\-password
\fIuser\fR [\fB\-data\fR \fIdir\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Virticle is one program that serves a web UI and API and manages libvirt
nodes over SSH. Nothing but a small node command is installed on the managed
nodes. The controller keeps its users, node list, task log and audit log in a
SQLite database in the data directory.
.PP
The package runs it as the systemd service
.B virticle.service
as user
.BR virticle ,
serving HTTPS with a self-signed certificate on port 8443. The package does
not change the firewall: run
.B sudo virticle setup
once. It opens the web port and prints the address to open to create the
administrator account.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B virticle
Run the controller.
.TP
.B virticle version
Print the version, commit and build date.
.TP
.B virticle setup
Run once as root after installing. Opens the web port in firewalld or ufw,
makes sure the service runs and prints the address to open. Running it again
changes nothing; after a change of the web port it moves the rule.
.B \-\-check
changes nothing.
.B \-\-undo
removes the firewall rule that setup added (do this before uninstalling).
.TP
.B virticle node prepare
Prepare a host as a node: installs libvirt, QEMU, the guest disk tools and the
node command, sets up the access the controller needs and opens the migration
ports (TCP 49152 to 49215) in firewalld or ufw. The controller signs in as the
account virticle\-node, which may run the node command as root and nothing
else.
.B \-\-root
gives it root instead.
.B \-\-check
changes nothing.
.B \-\-take\-over
answers yes when the node is managed by another Virticle controller (that
controller's key is removed).
.B \-\-jump
.I user@host
reaches the node through a jump host.
.B \-\-identity
.IR file ,
.B \-\-password\-stdin
choose how to sign in as administrator (default: the SSH agent). See
.B virticle node \-h
for all options.
.TP
.B virticle node unprepare
Undo prepare: removes the account, key, node command, sudo rule and firewall
rule. Packages, VMs, pools and networks stay.
.TP
.B virticle backup
Write the controller's own data (database, SSH key, certificates) to one file,
while the controller runs.
.B \-o
takes a file or a directory.
.B \-\-encrypt
asks for a passphrase (or reads it with
.BR \-\-passphrase\-file ).
.TP
.B virticle restore
Put such a file back. The controller must be stopped. An existing data
directory is moved aside, never overwritten.
.TP
.B virticle web
Read (\fBshow\fR), change (\fBset\fR) or reset to plain HTTP on
127.0.0.1:8080 (\fBreset\fR) the stored web access settings, for a headless
install or a locked\-out administrator. Restart the controller afterwards.
.TP
.B virticle user
Recover a sign\-in from the controller's machine:
.B reset\-2fa
turns two\-step sign\-in off for a user,
.B reset\-password
sets a new password for a local account. No restart is needed.
.SH OPTIONS
Run
.B virticle \-help
for the full list. The main flags of the controller are:
.TP
.BI \-listen " address"
Address to serve the web UI and API on. Given, it overrides the settings of
the Web access page. Without it, the stored settings decide; a new install
serves HTTPS with a self-signed certificate on port 8443, an installation
with users and no stored settings keeps 127.0.0.1:8080.
.TP
.BI \-data " dir"
Directory for the database and the controller's SSH key (default
/var/lib/virticle if it holds a database, else data).
.TP
.B \-no\-scheduler
Do not run scheduled snapshots and backups from this controller.
.TP
.B \-version
Print the version, commit and build date and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B VIRTICLE_JUMP_PASSWORD
Password for node jump hosts.
.TP
.B VIRTICLE_LISTEN
Default for \-listen.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/virticle/virticle.env
Service environment: VIRTICLE_ARGS (extra flags) and VIRTICLE_JUMP_PASSWORD.
Kept across upgrades.
.TP
.I /var/lib/virticle
Data directory: virticle.db, id_ed25519, known_hosts, instance\-id, secret.key,
metrics.db, and certificates. Copies of the database made before a schema
upgrade are named
.IR virticle.db.bak\-<version>\-<time> .
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR /usr/share/doc/virticle/docs/install.md ,
.I /usr/share/doc/virticle/README.md
